# Lesson 2, from the Lesson 2 bidding exercise 3c (partner opens 1S), with the DQ swapped for a small diamond so it fits the 12-13 raise (Mike, 2026-11-20).
title: Partner opens 1♠: a strong raise
id: L02-24
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.3, 2.1
student: S
board: 24
dealer: W
vulnerable: none

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  AK863  Q72    A4     Q93
  E  7      JT94   JT2    AT872
  S  QJ54   A      98763  KJ4
  W  T92    K8653  KQ5    65

auction:
  W Pass
  N 1S     = 13+ points, at least four spades
  E Pass
  S 3S*    = 12-13 points and four spades: forcing to game
     key: 11 HCP plus 2 for the singleton heart is 13, with four spades. That's the 3♠ raise.
     not 2S: 2♠ shows 6-9. Did you count the singleton? It brings you to 13.
     not 2D: You have four spades. Isn't the raise the first thing to show?
     not 4S: 4♠ isn't in our system. 3♠ shows the fit and game values, and partner will bid game.
     not *: With four spades and 12-13 points, which raise shows both?
  W Pass
  N 4S     = Game
  E Pass
  S Pass*  = Partner has chosen the game
     key: Your side has the points and the fit for game, and partner bid it. Pass.
     not *: We won't worry about slams yet. Partner bid game: pass.
  W Pass

auction recap:
  Your singleton heart is worth more now that you know partner has spades:
  four trumps and a short suit make a strong hand stronger. 3♠ showed
  four-card support and game values, and partner bid game. North is
  declarer, because she bid spades first, and so East will lead to the
  first trick.

play:
  1   E HJ  S HA  W H3  N H2
  2   S CK  W C5  N C3  E CA
      note: Declarer's plan: trump hearts in dummy, losing one trick in each side suit. First drive out the ♣A.
  3   E C2  S C4  W C6  N CQ
  4   N H7  E H4  S S4  W H5
      note: Dummy trumps a heart.
  5   S SQ  W S2  N S3  E S7
      note: A trump from dummy.
  6   S D3  W DQ  N DA  E D2
      note: A diamond to declarer's ace.
  7   N HQ  E H9  S SJ  W H6
      note: Dummy trumps another heart.
  8   S S5  W S9  N SK  E C7
      note: Now draw trumps.
  9   N SA  E DT  S D6  W ST
      note: The last trump.
  10  N C9  E CT  S CJ  W H8
      note: A club to dummy's ♣J.
  11  S D7  W DK  N D4  E DJ
      note: Give up a diamond.
  12  W HK  N S6  E HT  S D8
      note: Declarer trumps.
  13  N S8  E C8  S D9  W D5
      note: The last trump. 11 tricks: 4♠ made with an overtrick.

play recap:
  Declarer's plan: trump hearts in dummy, losing just one trick in each
  side suit.

  4♠ made with an overtrick. Your singleton heart let dummy ruff twice,
  just as the lesson says: a short suit gains value once you find a fit.
